      "content": "thanks for the list. none of those feel quite right though. when i think about these memories, it's not really about being a socialite or a writer... it's more about the weight of secrets. i remember sitting in these dimly lit offices, feeling this intense pressure to navigate these tiny, life-altering political shifts between France and the rest of Europe. it feels very strategic, very quiet, and very high-stakes. more like someone working behind the scenes in the government or a high-level embassy. do you have anyone in mind who was more of a heavy hitter in actual political maneuvering back then?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
